A declaration shadows an enum constant.

WHAT IT IS. Eight lines of legal C, and micro-c segfaults on them:

    enum { V = 7 };
    int main(void) { int V; V = 2; return V; }

primary_expr consulted global_constant_list BEFORE any variable list, so `V`
resolved to the literal 7 -- and `V = 2` then STORED THROUGH THE CONSTANT 7 as
if it were an address.

THE FIX. name_is_a_variable() runs the same lookups, in the same order, that
load_address_of_variable_into_register performs, and reports whether they would
find anything -- without emitting. The decision is then made before either path
commits.

`function` is NULL at file scope, which is exactly where an enum constant
SHOULD win, and it is tested rather than assumed. The alternative -- reordering
the two lookups -- would have been shorter and wrong: at file scope there is no
`function` to search and the deref would have faulted.

WHERE IT CAME FROM. Row 320 of stage 2's conformance corpus. pico-c compiles
it. It is a construct nobody working on this compiler would have thought to
write, which is the entire argument for borrowing a corpus written against a
different rung: the case suite in tools/cases/ was built FROM bugs already
found, so it measures what has been fixed rather than what remains.

WHETHER IT MATTERS FOR tcc: no. tcc does not shadow an enum constant anywhere.
That is stated because the previous two patches in this series were also not on
tcc's path, and a run of fixes that do not move the subject is worth naming as
such rather than letting the count of green cases imply progress.

MEASURED

    difftest      57 -> 58 pass, both architectures, nothing regressed
    corpus        422 -> 423 of 426 on aarch64
    vocabulary    clean on five architectures
    tcc           compiles, links and runs as before; the fault has NOT moved

diff --git a/cc_core.c b/cc_core.c
index 2a9e615..358b880 100644
--- a/cc_core.c
+++ b/cc_core.c
@@ -925,6 +925,34 @@ void primary_expr_number(char* s)
 	current_target = integer;
 }
 
+/* IS THIS NAME A VARIABLE? Asked WITHOUT emitting anything.
+ *
+ * A DECLARATION SHADOWS AN ENUM CONSTANT, and this compiler did not know it:
+ *
+ *     enum { V = 7 };
+ *     int main(void) { int V; V = 2; return V; }
+ *
+ * The constant list was consulted before any variable list, so `V` resolved to
+ * the literal 7 -- and `V = 2` then STORED THROUGH THE CONSTANT 7 as if it
+ * were an address. SIGSEGV, on eight lines of legal C that pico-c compiles.
+ *
+ * The lookups below are the same ones, in the same order, that
+ * load_address_of_variable_into_register performs; this one only reports
+ * whether they would find anything, so the decision can be made before either
+ * path emits. `function` is NULL at file scope, which is exactly where an enum
+ * constant SHOULD win, and is checked rather than assumed. */
+int name_is_a_variable(char* s)
+{
+	if(NULL != static_variable_lookup(s)) return TRUE;
+	if(NULL != function)
+	{
+		if(NULL != sym_lookup(s, function->locals)) return TRUE;
+		if(NULL != sym_lookup(s, function->arguments)) return TRUE;
+	}
+	if(NULL != sym_lookup(s, global_symbol_list)) return TRUE;
+	return FALSE;
+}
+
 struct token_list* load_address_of_variable_into_register(int reg, char* s)
 {
 	struct token_list* variable = static_variable_lookup(s);
@@ -1330,8 +1358,9 @@ void primary_expr_variable(void)
 		return;
 	}
 
+	/* A VARIABLE OF THE SAME NAME WINS -- see name_is_a_variable above. */
 	struct token_list* a = sym_lookup(s, global_constant_list);
-	if(NULL != a)
+	if(NULL != a && !name_is_a_variable(s))
 	{
 		emit_load_immediate(REGISTER_ZERO, strtolong(a->arguments->s), "constant load");
 		return;
